# Local-only fallback for `defineSecret()`-bound values, used by the
# Functions emulator whenever it can't reach Secret Manager (no `firebase
# login`, e.g. CI or a fresh contributor checkout) — this is the mechanism
# the emulator itself suggests in its own warning message. Committed
# (despite the generic `.secret.local` name normally implying a personal,
# gitignored file — see the exception in functions/.gitignore) because these
# are meaningless placeholders, never real credentials: `createCheckoutSession`
# only ever reaches code that reads STRIPE_SECRET_KEY when STRIPE_MOCK_CHECKOUT
# isn't set (see .env.demo-trivia-app-e2e + src/checkout-sessions.ts), which
# is never true for local/CI emulation.
#
# Testing locally against a REAL Stripe account through the emulator (rather
# than mock mode) requires deleting or renaming this file first, so the
# emulator falls through to real Secret Manager access instead.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_placeholder_never_used_in_mock_mode
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_placeholder_never_used_in_mock_mode
